3. Institutional Integration and Governance

MWTL functions as an ecosystem integrator, not a standalone facility. The anchor partners are:

· UM6P International Water Research Institute (IWRI): Provides physical testbeds, including the Green Energy Park and LIMSET.
· MASCIR Foundation: Contributes rural wastewater treatment expertise and software tools for water and renewable energy optimization.
· IAV Hassan II: Hosts doctoral research on hydraulic network design, irrigation performance, and water quality.
· ORMVA Souss-Massa: Manages irrigation water distribution and provides farmer network access.
· ABH Souss-Massa: Ensures regulatory compliance under Law 36-15 and data usability for basin planning.

3.1 Independent Scientific Committee

The independent scientific committee shall have five voting members:

· two Moroccan researchers nominated by UM6P and IAV Hassan II;
· two US researchers nominated by the US partner institution;
· one independent international chair with no institutional stake in the pilot.

The committee has decision rights over protocol amendments, data release, publication, and stop/scale recommendations. It has unrestricted access to raw data. No political objective shall override its scientific judgment.

3.2 Data Ownership and Intellectual Property

Raw data are owned by the research consortium. Aggregated data are shared with ABH and ORMVA for basin planning. Background IP remains with the originating partner. Foreground IP arising from the pilot is jointly owned by Moroccan and US partners, with licensing terms negotiated prior to commercialization. Publication rights are preserved for academic partners, subject to a 30-day review for confidential information.

3.3 Regulatory and Permitting

ABH Souss-Massa engagement begins at least six months before deployment. Deliverables include water withdrawal permits, Law 36-15 compliance documentation, and data-sharing approvals. Permit delays are treated as a schedule risk.

