5.4 Value Creation — Annual

Water savings at 25% efficiency gain:

\Delta W = 350{,}000 \times 0.25 = 87{,}500 \text{ m}^3/\text{year}.

At 10 MAD/m³, the potential financial saving is

875{,}000 \text{ MAD/year}.

Energy savings at 25% pumping reduction:

\Delta E = 105{,}000 \times 0.25 = 26{,}250 \text{ MAD/year}.

Yield uplift is provisionally set at 100,000 MAD/year. This must be derived, not assumed. If baseline yield is Y tonnes/ha, price is p MAD/tonne, and packout improves by \Delta \pi, then

\Delta R_y = A \cdot Y \cdot \Delta \pi \cdot p,

where A = 50 ha. For example, with Y = 40 t/ha, p = 3{,}000 MAD/t, and \Delta \pi = 0.04,

\Delta R_y = 50 \times 40 \times 0.04 \times 3{,}000 = 240{,}000 \text{ MAD/year}.

The 100,000 MAD figure is therefore conservative. It should be treated as a secondary endpoint to be measured, not as a guaranteed cash flow.

Gross annual financial value is

V_{\text{gross}} = 875{,}000 + 26{,}250 + 100{,}000 = 1{,}001{,}250 \text{ MAD}.

Net annual cash flow is

\text{NCF} = V_{\text{gross}} - \text{OPEX} = 1{,}001{,}250 - 250{,}000 = 751{,}250 \text{ MAD}.

5.5 Cash Savings versus Economic Water Value

Let \lambda \in [0,1] denote the fraction of conserved water that translates into cash savings. Then

\text{NCF}(\lambda) = \lambda \times 875{,}000 + 26{,}250 + 100{,}000 - 250{,}000.

For volumetric pricing, \lambda = 1:

\text{NCF}(1) = 751{,}250 \text{ MAD}.

For quota-constrained systems, \lambda = 0:

\text{NCF}(0) = -123{,}750 \text{ MAD}.

If yield uplift is also not realized, \text{NCF}(0) = -223{,}750 MAD. The base case is therefore conditional on volumetric pricing. In quota-constrained systems, conserved water must be valued at its shadow price, or the project must be justified by energy savings, yield protection, and optional expansion.

5.6 Financial Metrics

Simple payback with net CAPEX:

\text{Payback} = \frac{980{,}000}{751{,}250} = 1.304 \text{ years} = 15.7 \text{ months}.

Simple payback with gross CAPEX and no subsidy:

\text{Payback} = \frac{1{,}400{,}000}{751{,}250} = 1.864 \text{ years} = 22.4 \text{ months}.

Five-year NPV at 8%:

\text{NPV} = -980{,}000 + 751{,}250 \times \frac{1-(1.08)^{-5}}{0.08}
= 2{,}019{,}524 \text{ MAD}.

Five-year IRR is approximately

\text{IRR} \approx 71.5\%.

With a 15% contingency added to net CAPEX, risk-adjusted net CAPEX is 1,190,000 MAD:

\text{Payback} = \frac{1{,}190{,}000}{751{,}250} = 1.58 \text{ years} = 19.0 \text{ months},

\text{NPV} = 2{,}999{,}524 - 1{,}190{,}000 = 1{,}809{,}524 \text{ MAD},

\text{IRR} \approx 56.4\%.

5.7 Sensitivity Analysis

Net annual cash flow under varying water costs and water savings, assuming proportional energy savings and constant yield uplift:

