8. Falsification Criteria and Decision Gates

A pilot shall be considered unsuccessful if:

1. Water savings are statistically insignificant (p > 0.05).
2. Agricultural output decreases by more than 5%.
3. Maintenance and support costs exceed 15% of gross annual value generated.
4. Sensor failure rate exceeds 10% per annum.
5. Energy consumption offsets water savings.
6. Farmers cannot operate the system without external technical support.
7. CAPEX payback exceeds 36 months.
8. Local manufacturing is economically uncompetitive.
9. Results cannot be replicated at a second site.

At the end of the pilot, there shall be only three possible outcomes: Scale, Modify, or Stop. No political objective shall override the experimental result.

