10. Conclusion

This document provides the complete implementation-ready design for the Morocco Water Technology Laboratory. It corrects the unit economics, strengthens the experimental protocol, expands operating costs, distinguishes cash savings from economic water value, and introduces a risk register. The corrected base case yields a net annual cash flow of 751,250 MAD, a simple payback of 1.30 years with subsidy and 1.86 years without, a 5-year net present value of 2,019,524 MAD at 8%, and an internal rate of return of approximately 71.5%. The central proposition remains: build one system, measure it rigorously, compare it with the baseline, and determine whether it creates real economic value. If the answer is yes, build the second system. Then the third. Then industrialize. Then export. Morocco becomes the laboratory. Africa becomes the potential market. The United States becomes a technological and financial partner. The experiment determines whether the model deserves to scale.

