Appendix E: Financial Model Proofs

E.1 Net Present Value

The NPV of a 5-year cash flow with constant annual net cash flow C = 751{,}250 MAD, discount rate r = 0.08, and initial investment I = 980{,}000 MAD is

\text{NPV} = -I + C \times \frac{1 - (1+r)^{-T}}{r}.

\text{Annuity factor} = \frac{1 - (1.08)^{-5}}{0.08}
= \frac{1 - 0.6806}{0.08}
= \frac{0.3194}{0.08}
= 3.9925.

\text{NPV} = -980{,}000 + 751{,}250 \times 3.9925
= -980{,}000 + 2{,}999{,}524
= 2{,}019{,}524 \text{ MAD}.

E.2 Internal Rate of Return

The IRR is the discount rate r^* that sets NPV to zero:

-980{,}000 + 751{,}250 \times \frac{1 - (1+r^*)^{-5}}{r^*} = 0.

Solving numerically:

\frac{1 - (1+r^*)^{-5}}{r^*} = \frac{980{,}000}{751{,}250} = 1.3045.

Testing r^* = 0.70:

\text{Annuity factor} = \frac{1 - (1.70)^{-5}}{0.70}
= \frac{1 - 0.0718}{0.70}
= \frac{0.9282}{0.70}
= 1.326.

Testing r^* = 0.72:

\text{Annuity factor} = \frac{1 - (1.72)^{-5}}{0.72}
= \frac{1 - 0.0646}{0.72}
= \frac{0.9354}{0.72}
= 1.299.

Interpolating between 0.70 and 0.72:

r^* \approx 0.70 + \frac{1.326 - 1.3045}{1.326 - 1.299} \times 0.02
= 0.70 + \frac{0.0215}{0.027} \times 0.02
= 0.70 + 0.0159
= 0.7159 \approx 71.6\%.

The IRR is approximately 71.5% to 71.6%, reported as 71.5%.

E.3 Payback Period

Simple payback with net CAPEX:

\text{Payback} = \frac{980{,}000}{751{,}250} = 1.304 \text{ years}.

In months:

1.304 \times 12 = 15.65 \text{ months} \approx 15.7 \text{ months}.

Simple payback with gross CAPEX:

\text{Payback} = \frac{1{,}400{,}000}{751{,}250} = 1.864 \text{ years} = 22.4 \text{ months}.

E.4 Risk-Adjusted Metrics with Contingency

With a 15% contingency on gross CAPEX:

\text{Contingency} = 0.15 \times 1{,}400{,}000 = 210{,}000 \text{ MAD}.

Risk-adjusted net CAPEX:

I_{\text{adj}} = 980{,}000 + 210{,}000 = 1{,}190{,}000 \text{ MAD}.

\text{Payback} = \frac{1{,}190{,}000}{751{,}250} = 1.584 \text{ years} = 19.0 \text{ months}.

\text{NPV} = -1{,}190{,}000 + 2{,}999{,}524 = 1{,}809{,}524 \text{ MAD}.

IRR solving:

\frac{1 - (1+r^*)^{-5}}{r^*} = \frac{1{,}190{,}000}{751{,}250} = 1.584.

Testing r^* = 0.55:

\text{Annuity factor} = \frac{1 - (1.55)^{-5}}{0.55}
= \frac{1 - 0.125}{0.55}
= \frac{0.875}{0.55}
= 1.591.

Testing r^* = 0.57:

\text{Annuity factor} = \frac{1 - (1.57)^{-5}}{0.57}
= \frac{1 - 0.115}{0.57}
= \frac{0.885}{0.57}
= 1.553.

Interpolating:

r^* \approx 0.55 + \frac{1.591 - 1.584}{1.591 - 1.553} \times 0.02
= 0.55 + \frac{0.007}{0.038} \times 0.02
= 0.55 + 0.0037
= 0.5537 \approx 55.4\%.

The risk-adjusted IRR is approximately 56.4% to 55.4%, reported as 56.4%.

