G.3 Data Quality Control

1. Range checks: Flag values outside physically plausible ranges (e.g., flow > 2× design capacity).
2. Spike detection: Flag values exceeding 3 standard deviations from a 24-hour rolling mean.
3. Gap filling: Linear interpolation for gaps < 2 hours; multiple imputation for longer gaps.
4. Calibration: Flow meters calibrated quarterly; soil moisture probes calibrated annually.
5. Audit trail: All data modifications logged with timestamp and user ID.

G.4 Analysis Plan

1. Primary analysis: ANCOVA of season-average water consumption on treatment, with baseline water use, soil type, and proximity to water source as covariates.
2. Repeated measures: Linear mixed-effects model with plot as random effect and season as repeated factor.
3. Missing data: Multiple imputation under MAR; sensitivity analysis under MNAR.
4. Multiple testing: Benjamini–Hochberg for secondary endpoints.
5. Effect size: Standardized mean differences with 95% confidence intervals.
6. Intention-to-treat: All randomized plots analysed as assigned.

